<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Multi Hex Visualizer" description="Learn how Multi Hex Visualizer handles palette data, browser storage, shared links, and hosting information." path="/privacy/">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: November 22, 2026</p>
  <p>Multi Hex Visualizer is a browser-based color tool. This policy explains what information the application handles when you use it and what choices you have.</p>
  <h2>Palette and workspace data</h2>
  <p>The colors, group names, custom color names, and view settings you enter are processed in your browser. The application stores the current workspace in your browser’s local storage so it can be restored after a refresh or on a later visit from the same browser. This information is not submitted to an application account or database because the tool does not provide user accounts or a hosted workspace service.</p>
  <h2>Shared links and exported files</h2>
  <p>When you use the Share feature, workspace information is encoded into the URL fragment. URL fragments are normally handled by the browser and are not sent to a web server as part of the page request. Anyone who receives a shared link may be able to view the palette it contains, so do not include confidential names or information. Exported files are created for you to save and manage.</p>
  <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>The application does not set advertising cookies and does not include an account system. It uses local storage for workspace state and theme preference. The hosting provider may process standard technical logs—such as IP address, browser type, requested page, and request time—for security, reliability, or operational purposes under the provider’s own terms.</p>
  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>The site links to GitHub for source code, issue reports, and project feedback. When you follow an external link, the destination’s privacy policy applies. Multi Hex Visualizer does not control how third-party sites process data.</p>
  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You can remove saved workspace data by clearing this site’s local storage in your browser. You may also use a private browsing session if you do not want the browser to retain the workspace after the session ends. Deleting a shared link or exported file from your own devices does not remove copies previously sent to other people.</p>
  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>This policy may be updated when the tool or its hosting changes. The revision date at the top identifies the current version. For privacy questions, open an issue in the <a href="https://github.com/mshareef-git/Multi-Hex-Visualizer/issues">project’s GitHub issue tracker</a>.</p>
</Layout>
